{# viz_facts - the FACTS family of the data-viz PRESET layer: the two devices the
   reference decks lean on hardest.

     icon_stat_row  one sourced fact, in a ROW of 3-5 (the contract's `fakten`
                    shape). Frese p3 runs 5 across (500+ / 200+ / 10+ / 5 / 6),
                    Martic p5 runs 3 (87.8% / 45 / 47%).
     column_chart   a trend over time with the VALUE PRINTED ABOVE EACH BAR and
                    the last (or named) bar carrying the accent. Frese p5,
                    "Vakanzzeit-Treppe 2018-2025".

   Brand-agnostic / token-only: every colour arrives as var(--token), the glyphs
   come from icons.jinja and inherit currentColor, so neither macro carries a
   literal of its own. Macros take (v, uid=0), matching the rest of the viz
   families; the dispatch threads loop.index as uid. Neither macro emits an SVG
   id, gradient, or clip path, so two equal figures on one page cannot collide by
   construction.

   The two laws from the contract, enforced here:
     1. NOTHING IS FABRICATED. Every figure and source is printed VERBATIM as the
        writer supplied it. Bar geometry is DERIVED from the same string via the
        `num` filter, so a bar can never disagree with the numeral above it.
     2. GRACEFUL AT EVERY HOP. A missing field omits its element; an empty or
        unusable spec renders nothing at all. Adding a fact to a page can never
        break a render. #}
{% from 'icons.jinja' import icon %}

{# icon_stat_row - a row of 3-5 fact cards (1-6 handled). Per card: a circled
   line-icon, the big figure, a bold short label, the body text, and the source
   line pinned to the figure it belongs to (contract: "Every figure keeps its
   source INLINE, never detached").

   Cards are equal-width flex children that wrap only when they must. The figure
   steps DOWN the type ramp as the row gets denser (see [data-count] in viz.css):
   a 40pt numeral is right for 2 cards and overflows a 5-card column, so the
   count drives the tier. data-count carries the FILTERED card count, so the
   CSS sizes what is actually drawn.

   Graceful: a card with no `figur` is skipped (the figure IS the card); missing
   text/quelle omit their line; an unknown or absent `icon` key drops the whole
   badge rather than leaving an empty circle. `items` empty -> nothing renders. #}
{% macro icon_stat_row(v, uid=0) %}
{%- set items = (v.get('items') if v else none) or none -%}
{%- set cards = (items | selectattr('figur') | list) if items else [] -%}
{%- if cards -%}
<figure class="c-viz c-viz-facts" role="img" aria-label="{% for it in cards %}{{ it.figur }} {{ it.label or '' }}; {% endfor %}">
  <div class="c-viz-facts__row" data-count="{{ cards | length }}">
  {%- for it in cards -%}
    {%- set glyph = icon(it.icon, uid ~ '_' ~ loop.index) -%}
    <div class="c-viz-facts__card">
      {%- if glyph | trim %}<div class="c-viz-facts__badge">{{ glyph }}</div>{% endif -%}
      <div class="c-viz-facts__figur">{{ it.figur }}</div>
      {%- if it.label %}<div class="c-viz-facts__label">{{ it.label }}</div>{% endif -%}
      {%- if it.text %}<div class="c-viz-facts__text">{{ it.text }}</div>{% endif -%}
      {%- if it.quelle %}<div class="c-viz-facts__quelle">{{ it.quelle }}</div>{% endif -%}
    </div>
  {%- endfor -%}
  </div>
</figure>
{%- endif -%}
{% endmacro %}

{# column_chart - the trend device. Columns scaled to the max, each value printed
   ABOVE its bar, each label below, one bar in the accent.

   Geometry lives in a viewBox (0 0 320 180) with width:100%; height:auto, so the
   chart scales to whatever column it lands in and can never overflow a fixed mm
   height in print. Bars: baseline y=160, tallest bar 130 units, band = 320/n,
   bar width 52% of its band capped at 34 units so a 2-point chart does not draw
   two slabs. Text sizes are set in viz.css and land in USER units, so they scale
   with the viewBox exactly like the donut's centre figure.

   `wert` may be a German-formatted string ("1.200", "2,5"): the `num` filter
   parses it (thousands dot, decimal comma) and the SAME string is printed
   verbatim above the bar, so geometry and numeral cannot diverge. An entry whose
   `wert` carries no digit at all is SKIPPED (a bar we cannot size is a bar we
   must not invent).

   `hervorheben` picks the accent bar: a string matches a point's `label`, an
   integer indexes the DRAWN bars (identical to the input index unless an entry
   was skipped), and the default is the LAST bar (the trend's punchline). An
   out-of-range index falls back to the default rather than dropping the accent.

   `einheit` is appended to each value when it is short (<= 4 chars, e.g. "%",
   "Tage"); a longer unit becomes a caption under the title instead of bloating
   every label. Graceful: no usable points -> nothing renders. #}
{% macro column_chart(v, uid=0) %}
{%- set punkte = (v.get('punkte') if v else none) or none -%}
{%- set pts = [] -%}
{%- if punkte -%}
  {%- for p in punkte if p -%}
    {%- if (p.wert | string | list | select('in', '0123456789') | list | length) > 0 -%}
      {%- set _ = pts.append(p) -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- if pts -%}
{%- set n = pts | length -%}
{%- set m = pts | map(attribute='wert') | map('num') | list | max -%}
{%- set base = 160 -%}
{%- set maxh = 130 -%}
{%- set band = 320.0 / n -%}
{%- set bw = [band * 0.52, 34] | min -%}
{%- set einheit = v.get('einheit') -%}
{%- set unit_inline = einheit if (einheit and (einheit | string | length) <= 4) else '' -%}
{%- set hl = namespace(i = n - 1) -%}
{%- set hv = v.get('hervorheben') -%}
{%- if hv is not none -%}
  {%- if hv is number -%}
    {%- if (hv | int) >= 0 and (hv | int) < n -%}{%- set hl.i = hv | int -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- for p in pts -%}
      {%- if (p.label | string) == (hv | string) -%}{%- set hl.i = loop.index0 -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
<figure class="c-viz c-viz-col" role="img" aria-label="{{ v.titel or '' }} {% for p in pts %}{{ p.label or '' }}: {{ p.wert }} {{ einheit or '' }}; {% endfor %}">
  {%- if v.titel %}<figcaption class="c-viz-col__title">{{ v.titel }}</figcaption>{% endif -%}
  {%- if einheit and not unit_inline %}<div class="c-viz-col__unit">{{ einheit }}</div>{% endif -%}
  <svg class="c-viz-col__svg" viewBox="0 0 320 180">
  {%- for p in pts -%}
    {%- set val = p.wert | num -%}
    {%- set h = ([(val / m * maxh), 3] | max) if (m and val > 0) else 0 -%}
    {%- set y = base - h -%}
    {%- set cx = band * (loop.index0 + 0.5) -%}
    {%- set is_hl = ' is-hl' if loop.index0 == hl.i else '' -%}
    <rect class="c-viz-col__bar{{ is_hl }}" x="{{ (cx - bw / 2) | round(2) }}" y="{{ y | round(2) }}" width="{{ bw | round(2) }}" height="{{ h | round(2) }}"/>
    <text class="c-viz-col__val{{ is_hl }}" x="{{ cx | round(2) }}" y="{{ (y - 4.5) | round(2) }}" text-anchor="middle">{{ p.wert }}{{ ' ' ~ unit_inline if unit_inline }}</text>
    {%- if p.label %}<text class="c-viz-col__xlab" x="{{ cx | round(2) }}" y="{{ base + 14 }}" text-anchor="middle">{{ p.label }}</text>{% endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
    <line class="c-viz-col__axis" x1="0" y1="{{ base }}" x2="320" y2="{{ base }}"/>
  </svg>
  {%- if v.quelle %}<figcaption class="c-viz-col__quelle">{{ v.quelle }}</figcaption>{% endif -%}
</figure>
{%- endif -%}
{% endmacro %}
